  "changed_factors": [
    "Set prior_update=frozen and prior_code_law=fresh_gaussian: every sampled latent is a fresh init_std * N(0, I) code of the task's latent dimension (init_std is 1 on every task in this suite), drawn from the task's existing prior-noise stream (else the latent stream); the uniform row indices are still drawn from the latent-index stream exactly as before. Capacity matching: same z_dim, the same number of latent draws per update and per evaluation, and the same marginal scale as the task's initial table; the only difference from the frozen-table arm is unbounded support (fresh draws) instead of a finite table. Hosts that enumerate, encode against or optimize table rows are explicitly BLOCKED. Everything else is the selected BISPF recipe bispf-optimized-quintic-v1 unchanged: Born-Infeld critic, optimizer, rates, momentum, schedules, thermal behaviour, shape/step gates, architecture, initialization, data, batch sequence and sampling."
